    "long_instructions": "###Producing CSS\r\nUsing AI, produce a CSS file for a webpage about dogs. \r\n\r\n## Steps \r\n1. Add your HTML file from level 11 using the `+` next to Files.\r\n\t- Select import from backback\r\n    - Select the correct file using the drop down\r\n    - Click `Import to Project`\r\n    - *notice there are now two files: an HTML file and a CSS file*\r\n2. Switch to AI mode and ask the AI to spruce up your dog website with some CSS.\r\n3. Copy and paste the code to the `styles.css` file. \r\n4. Feel free to go back and forth with the AI improving the site as much as you like. \r\n\r\n## Debug \r\nYou will notice that the CSS doesn't automatically show up in the preview. \r\nAsk the AI to help you debug. \r\n\r\n::: details [**🔎 Show me how**]\r\nThe common error here is that the `CSS` File is not linked to the `HTML` file. \r\nAdd \r\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"styles.css\">\r\nto the head section of your 'HTML' file\r\n\r\n![](https://images.code.org/03cf50f51e34a0c0abd83c1d6c4a6a21-image-1761073206253.png)\r\n:::\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n",
